** requires: marmot-module AT2PhaseField
** requires: marmot-module GeneralGradientEnhancedDisplacementFiniteElement

** Live 2D h-adaptivity of a two-field (displacement + nonlocal damage) model, the 2D counterpart of
** AMR_TwoFieldGC3D20R: a distorted GCPE8R cantilever (plane strain, thickness 2) under an end displacement.
** After the first increment the stress marker refines the elements at the clamped end, so the second
** increment solves with hanging nodes that couple both fields, the damage state transferred to the
** children (2D inverse map of the state transfer) and both fields warm-started at the new nodes.
*material, name=AT2PHASEFIELD, id=mat
20000, 0.2, 0.1, 5

*section, name=sec, material=mat, type=plane, thickness=2.0
all

*modelModifier, type=hAdaptivity, name=amr
>>marker, type=fieldOutput, fieldOutput=stressForAMR, operator='>', threshold=7.0
maxLevel=1

*job, name=amr, domain=2d
*solver, solver=NIST, name=S
*fieldOutput
>>perNode, elSet=all, field=displacement, result=U, name=U
>>perNode, elSet=all, field=nonlocal damage, result=U, name=D
>>perElement, elSet=all, result=stress, quadraturePoint=0:4, name=stressForAMR, f(x)='np.abs(x)'

*step, solver=S
maxInc=0.8, minInc=0.2, maxNumInc=2, maxIter=25
>>dirichlet, name=left, nSet=left, field=displacement, 1=0.0, 2=0.0
>>dirichlet, name=right, nSet=right, field=displacement, 2=-0.003

*node
